.\" File generated from our OpenAPI spec by Scalar. Do not edit.
.TH "DEVCLI" "1" "" "devcli" "Demo API (Scalar Galaxy) Manual"
.SH "NAME"
devcli \- command line interface for the Demo API (Scalar Galaxy)
.SH "SYNOPSIS"
.B devcli
[\fIglobal options\fR] \fIcommand\fR [\fIsubcommand\fR] [\fIarguments\fR] [\fIoptions\fR]
.SH "DESCRIPTION"
devcli calls the Demo API (Scalar Galaxy) from the command line. Commands are grouped by resource, and every command prints its result to standard output in the configured format.
.PP
The Scalar Galaxy is an example OpenAPI document to test OpenAPI tools and libraries. It's a fictional universe with fictional planets and fictional data.
.SH "GLOBAL OPTIONS"
.TP
\fB\-\-base\-url\fR \fI<url>\fR
Override the base URL for API requests.
.TP
\fB\-\-timeout\fR \fI<ms>\fR
Request timeout in milliseconds.
.TP
\fB\-\-max\-retries\fR \fI<count>\fR
Number of retries for retryable failures.
.TP
\fB\-\-format\fR \fI<format>\fR
Output format: auto, json, jsonl, pretty, raw, toon, yaml.
.TP
\fB\-\-format\-error\fR \fI<format>\fR
Error output format: auto, json, jsonl, pretty, raw, toon, yaml.
.TP
\fB\-\-transform\fR \fI<path>\fR
Dot\-path transform for data output.
.TP
\fB\-\-transform\-error\fR \fI<path>\fR
Dot\-path transform for error output.
.TP
\fB\-r\fR, \fB\-\-raw\-output\fR
Print transformed string values without JSON quotes.
.TP
\fB\-\-debug\fR
Enable SDK debug logging on standard error.
.TP
\fB\-\-environment\fR \fI<name>\fR
Named environment to target: production, responds_with_your_request_data (can also be set with DEMO_API_SCALAR_GALAXY_ENVIRONMENT env var) (default: production). Cannot be combined with \-\-base\-url.
.TP
\fB\-\-bearer\-auth\fR \fI<value>\fR
JWT Bearer token authentication. Can also be set with the BEARER_AUTH environment variable.
.TP
\fB\-\-basic\-auth\-username\fR \fI<value>\fR
Basic HTTP authentication. Can also be set with the BASIC_AUTH_USERNAME environment variable.
.TP
\fB\-\-basic\-auth\-password\fR \fI<value>\fR
Basic HTTP authentication. Can also be set with the BASIC_AUTH_PASSWORD environment variable.
.TP
\fB\-\-api\-key\-header\fR \fI<value>\fR
API key request header. Can also be set with the API_KEY_HEADER environment variable.
.TP
\fB\-\-api\-key\-query\fR \fI<value>\fR
API key query parameter. Can also be set with the API_KEY_QUERY environment variable.
.TP
\fB\-\-api\-key\-cookie\fR \fI<value>\fR
API key browser cookie. Can also be set with the API_KEY_COOKIE environment variable.
.TP
\fB\-\-o\-auth2\fR \fI<value>\fR
OAuth 2.0 authentication. Can also be set with the DEMO_API_SCALAR_GALAXY_O_AUTH2 environment variable.
.TP
\fB\-\-open\-id\-connect\fR \fI<value>\fR
OpenID Connect Authentication. Can also be set with the DEMO_API_SCALAR_GALAXY_OPEN_ID_CONNECT environment variable.
.SH "COMMANDS"
.TP
\fBdevcli planets list\-all\-data\fR
Get all planets. See devcli\-planets\-list\-all\-data(1).
.TP
\fBdevcli planets create\fR
Create a planet. See devcli\-planets\-create(1).
.TP
\fBdevcli planets retrieve\fR
Get a planet. See devcli\-planets\-retrieve(1).
.TP
\fBdevcli planets update\fR
Update a planet. See devcli\-planets\-update(1).
.TP
\fBdevcli planets delete\fR
Delete a planet. See devcli\-planets\-delete(1).
.TP
\fBdevcli planets upload\-image\fR
Upload an image to a planet. See devcli\-planets\-upload\-image(1).
.TP
\fBdevcli celestial\-bodies create\fR
Create a celestial body. See devcli\-celestial\-bodies\-create(1).
.TP
\fBdevcli authentication create\-user\fR
Create a user. See devcli\-authentication\-create\-user(1).
.TP
\fBdevcli authentication create\-token\fR
Get a token. See devcli\-authentication\-create\-token(1).
.TP
\fBdevcli authentication list\-me\fR
Get authenticated user. See devcli\-authentication\-list\-me(1).
.TP
\fBdevcli environments\fR
List the named environments \-\-environment can select. See devcli\-environments(1).
.TP
\fBdevcli completion\fR
Print a shell completion script. See devcli\-completion(1).
.TP
\fBdevcli login\fR
Sign in and save credentials for later commands. See devcli\-login(1).
.TP
\fBdevcli logout\fR
Forget saved credentials. See devcli\-logout(1).
.TP
\fBdevcli upgrade\fR
Upgrade to the latest release, through the package manager that owns this installation when one does. See devcli\-upgrade(1).
.TP
\fBdevcli uninstall\fR
Print how to remove this installation. See devcli\-uninstall(1).
.SH "ENVIRONMENTS"
\-\-environment selects one of these base URLs, or DEMO_API_SCALAR_GALAXY_ENVIRONMENT when the flag is not passed, and production is used when neither is. Run devcli environments to print the same list.
.TP
\fBproduction\fR
https://galaxy.scalar.com (default)
.TP
\fBresponds_with_your_request_data\fR
{protocol}://void.scalar.com/{path}
.SH "FILE ARGUMENTS"
Any command flag or credential reads its value from a file when the value begins with @. A flag shown with a <path> value uploads a file and takes its path with or without the @. The global options above are read exactly as written.
.PP
.RS 4
.nf
devcli COMMAND \-\-FLAG @./body.json    # contents of the file
devcli COMMAND \-\-FLAG @file://./n.txt # always sent as text
devcli COMMAND \-\-FLAG @data://./l.png # always base64\-encoded
devcli COMMAND \-\-FLAG '\e@literal'    # a value that begins with @
.fi
.RE
.SH "SHELL COMPLETION"
devcli completion <shell> prints a completion script for bash, zsh, and fish. Load it from your shell startup file:
.PP
.RS 4
.nf
eval "$(devcli completion bash)"
eval "$(devcli completion zsh)"
devcli completion fish | source
.fi
.RE
.SH "ENVIRONMENT"
.TP
\fBDEMO_API_SCALAR_GALAXY_ENVIRONMENT\fR
Fallback for \-\-environment when the flag is not passed. Ignored when \-\-base\-url is passed, and refused beside the base URL environment variable.
.TP
\fBBEARER_AUTH\fR
Fallback for \-\-bearer\-auth when the flag is not passed.
.TP
\fBBASIC_AUTH_USERNAME\fR
Fallback for \-\-basic\-auth\-username when the flag is not passed.
.TP
\fBBASIC_AUTH_PASSWORD\fR
Fallback for \-\-basic\-auth\-password when the flag is not passed.
.TP
\fBAPI_KEY_HEADER\fR
Fallback for \-\-api\-key\-header when the flag is not passed.
.TP
\fBAPI_KEY_QUERY\fR
Fallback for \-\-api\-key\-query when the flag is not passed.
.TP
\fBAPI_KEY_COOKIE\fR
Fallback for \-\-api\-key\-cookie when the flag is not passed.
.TP
\fBDEMO_API_SCALAR_GALAXY_O_AUTH2\fR
Fallback for \-\-o\-auth2 when the flag is not passed.
.TP
\fBDEMO_API_SCALAR_GALAXY_OPEN_ID_CONNECT\fR
Fallback for \-\-open\-id\-connect when the flag is not passed.
.SH "EXIT STATUS"
.TP
\fB0\fR
The command completed successfully.
.TP
\fB1\fR
The request failed for an unclassified reason. Reported as error.
.TP
\fB2\fR
The command was invoked incorrectly (missing or invalid arguments).
.TP
\fB10\fR
Authentication or authorization failed (HTTP 401 or 403). Reported as auth\-failed.
.TP
\fB11\fR
The requested resource does not exist (HTTP 404). Reported as not\-found.
.TP
\fB12\fR
The request was rate limited (HTTP 429). Reported as rate\-limited.
.TP
\fB13\fR
The request was rejected (any other HTTP 4xx). Reported as client\-error.
.TP
\fB14\fR
The API failed to handle the request (HTTP 5xx). Reported as server\-error.
.TP
\fB15\fR
The API could not be reached, or the request timed out. Reported as connection\-error.
